invariant: INV-41
file: webpki.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh rsa-ifma-callers
reason: the chain walk verifies a certificate's signature under the key of
  the issuer the peer sent with 0 in place of the session's ch_cfg.cpu,
  so a session whose caller set CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA runs that public
  operation on rsa_mont64.c. The verdict is the same.
  test/webpki_auth_ifma.h requires three calls to rsa_ifma_public from the
  aws chain's flight under a value with the bit, one of them the leaf's
  signature under the RSA-2048 intermediate. Only an x86-64 object makes
  the call, so test/aes-runtime-qemu.sh builds bin/webpki_auth_host for
  x86-64 and runs it under qemu-x86_64. The lane skips without docker, and
  this then reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
        rc = read_issuer(CH_CFG_CPU(*cfg), &entries, read, below, now, &cert, &issuer, alert);
--- new
        rc = read_issuer(0U, &entries, read, below, now, &cert, &issuer, alert);
